      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Even if you received a tetanus shot previously, injuries from rusty metal still warrant a doctor's check, as immunity can fade. Do not soak the wound in alcohol, as this can damage your tissue and cause more pain. Focus on keeping the wound clean with mild soap and running water, and cover it with a sterile bandage. However, for peace of mind and to rule out other infections, seeking medical advice remains the safest choice.",
      "source": "target",
